            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative efficiency of a course of multi-factor physiotherapeutic treatment and a complex of instrumental physiotherapy technics for medical rehabilitation of patients with stable angina pectoris].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Examination of comparable groups of patients with angina of efforts has demonstrated identical clinical efficiency of multi-factor therapeutic modalities and methods of instrumental physiotherapy for medical rehabilitation of patients with stable angina of effort. The results of this study suggest the possibility to avoid polypragmasia when prescribing physiotherapeutic treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
